}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Shirou Emiya CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Shirou Emiya is disgustingly powerful. His main attack consists of two closely spaced Multi-Hits, with each creating a level 4 [[Wave Attack]] that reaches up to 933 range. This splits his 204k effective burst damage (362k at Lv.50) between four hits. Because of this, the second half of his Multi-Hit has a tendency to miss if the first hit and Wave end up staggering every enemy. This sometimes makes him inconsistent to use, as there's a chance one or more of these hits end up missing. Each individual hit is still very strong, regardless of how many connect. While he is indeed less effective against Wave Immune threats, many backline enemies that aren't will still be easily decimated, with [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Professor A.]] being prime examples.

At his highest potential, Shirou's DPS is ludicrous. To put things into perspective, a Lv.60 [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Stroller]] deals ~22,375 DPS, which is already on the upper end for Wavers; Shirou exceeds this threshold at merely Lv.43, assuming everything connects. This is without mentioning the fact that he is a superbackliner with '''560 range''', further complemented by decent survivability through his base HP and knockback count (although Stroller has an advantage in disposability). With all of this in mind, the aim of the game is to lure as many enemies into his attacking range by the time he finishes his drawn-out foreswing animation. The tankier the enemies, the better his overall output is. Try to consider his matchups carefully so that he doesn't whiff Multi-Hits as often, especially given his 12.5-second attack cycle—not that it holds him back much either way.

Shirou's immunities are nothing to write home about, but [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback]] and [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] do give him a better matchup in stages containing [[Mr. Mole]] and [[Henry]] respectively. He does require extensive protection due to his long recharge time.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Waver & Super-Backliner}}

